      "severity": "critical",
      "body": "**Stored XSS:** `escapeHtml` was removed and `body` is passed straight into `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Any comment payload such as `<img src=x onerror=...>` or `<script>` executes in every viewer\u2019s session (cookie/token theft, forged actions, defacement).\n\nThere is no sanitizer or markdown renderer in this repo to replace the removed escape. Restore escaping, or render rich text via a safe path (markdown\u2192React elements, or DOMPurify/equivalent with a strict allowlist) before using `__html`."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "## Verdict\n\n**Critical XSS regression** \u2014 do not merge until comment HTML is sanitized or rendered safely.\n\n## What changed\n\n`Comment` still uses `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, but this PR deletes the only guard (`escapeHtml`) and feeds the raw `body` string straight into the DOM. There is no markdown parser, allowlist, or sanitizer (e.g. DOMPurify) elsewhere in the tree; this component is the full surface.\n\n## Failure mode\n\nAny comment author who can supply `body` can inject arbitrary HTML/JS, for example:\n\n```html\n<img src=x onerror=\"alert(document.cookie)\">\n```\n\nor a full `<script>` / event-handler payload. That steals sessions, performs actions as the viewer, and defaces the thread \u2014 the exact class of bug `escapeHtml` was preventing.\n\n## Safe paths to rich formatting\n\n- Parse a **restricted** markdown subset to React elements (no raw HTML), or\n- Keep `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` only after a vetted sanitizer with a tight allowlist (tags/attrs for bold + links), or\n- Render plain text / React children and style bold/links without HTML injection.\n\n## Release decision\n\n**Recommendation:** request-changes\n",
